		(uuid a8b7c4ed-6625-5b1a-bb3f-a564bb375bca)
	)
	(text "1. All components are through-hole. U1 plugs into two 1x15 female headers, U2 into a DIP-14 socket.\n2. Measure the ESP32 header row spacing before the PCB layout (footprint assumes 25.4 mm) and check the\n   board silkscreen matches the U1 pin labels (DOIT DevKit V1 30-pin layout).\n3. High-current path: J1 -> F1 -> Q1 -> J2. Use wide copper pours, 2 oz copper, and both poles of J1/J2\n   in parallel above ~10A. Use 14AWG (12AWG at 20A) wire. Each 5.08 mm terminal pole is rated ~13.5A.\n   Long strips: inject power at both ends, taken from J2.\n4. One common ground: PSU, LED strip, ESP32 and Raspberry Pi. Run the J3 GND wire alongside DATA.\n5. LED data: GPIO2 -> U2A (SN74AHCT125N, must be AHCT) -> R9 330 Ohm -> strip DIN.\n6. Firmware: pio run -e WS281x_RGB_LED_POWER  (LED_POWER_PIN=16, active-high, no LED_POWER_INVERT).\n7. Q1: Goford G75P04T (-40V, Rds(on) max 9 mOhm @ Vgs -4.5V, pins G-D-S). Any TO-220 P-MOSFET specified\n   for Vgs = -4.5V also works. IRF4905/IRF9540 are NOT suitable (not logic-level).\n8. Raspberry Pi 5 is powered through GPIO 5V pins: its USB ports are limited to 600 mA unless\n   usb_max_current_enable=1 is set in config.txt (only if the PSU can supply it).\n9. HyperHDR: keep Smoothing enabled so static images are resent (inactivity timeout)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 182.88 134.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid 1e2808bf-59c0-57c5-899d-cf483b9db954)
	)
